  "description": "SkySat imagery acquired 19 October 2026 over the area east of the Rasuwa (Bhote Koshi–Trishuli) corridor, around 28.3N 85.5E, the same area covered by the late-September SkySat, Pelican and PlanetScope collections and by the 12 October Pelican collection. Two collects about 30 seconds apart (strips s109_20261019T092932Z and s109_20261019T093004Z), each with two scenes, acquired at 19 to 21 degrees off-nadir. About 20 to 22% of each scene is clear and about 31 to 34% is snow/ice. 4 scenes; each Item carries the available visual, pansharpened, udm assets.",
